#AUTO 22
#NEEDED 0
# usb-enum — actually RUN the EP0 enumeration bring-up and report where it gets.
#
# The SusPHY fix for the 109b hang lives in usb_endpoint_zero_bringup(), but
# that function is declared in 002-main.c and NEVER CALLED at boot — usb_init()
# brings the PHY + controller up and stops there. So a plain reflash exercises
# none of the enumeration path. This probe calls it from the sweep, where
# usb_init has already put the controller in device mode, with the bounded
# depcmd_issue as the safety net: a still-stuck endpoint command logs "[usb]
# DEPCMD stuck ..." and returns instead of hanging the whole sweep.
#
# What to read in the log after the sweep:
#   "GUSB2PHYCFG after ... SusPHY=0 (fix cleared it)"  -> the fix ran
#   no "[usb] DEPCMD stuck" lines                       -> commands completed
#   a "[usb] DEPCMD stuck" line                         -> still hung: the PHY
#       clock is dead for another reason (next suspect: the CRU
#       resetn_usb2phy0_por reset, which 009's usb2_phy_bring_up doesn't touch).
#
# No #WRITES marker needed: the register writes happen inside the C CALL target
# (like otp/rng/crypto), not through the DSL W command.
CALL usb_enum
